    "# Wealth-Inequality Change in the NLS 1979 Cohort (1990 -> 1996)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Question.** What changes occurred in the wealth inequality for white males and females between 1990 and 1996?\n",
    "\n",
    "**Approach.** Compute within-group inequality on white-female and white-male subgroups for both years (1990, 1996) on the raw data, using the Lorenz-curve Gini coefficient as the headline metric (with std, CV, IQR, P90/P50, and top-decile share as supporting measures). 1,000-iteration bootstrap percentile CIs are reported for all metrics.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Treatment rules.** Negatives are retained as debt; outliers are not deleted. Winsorized (1st/99th percentile) and ever_jailed=0 robustness variants are reported below.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": 1,
   "source": [
    "import json, numpy as np, pandas as pd\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "RNG = np.random.default_rng(20261021)\n",
    "BOOT_N = 1000\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv('/workspace/data/nls_incarceration_processed.csv')\n",
    "white = df[df['race']=='white'].copy()\n",
    "print('white N =', len(white))\n",
    "print('  female:', (white.sex=='female').sum())\n",
    "print('  male  :', (white.sex=='male').sum())\n"
   ],
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Lorenz-curve Gini and supporting metric functions\n",
    "\n",
    "Notes on the Gini: in heavy-tailed wealth data, the standard mean-diff Gini G = E|X-Y|/(2*mu) can exceed 1.0. We use the **Lorenz-curve Gini** (rank-based), bounded in [0,1] whenever total sum is positive (true here). Observations with negative net wealth sit at the bottom of the cumulative-wealth Lorenz curve. A n/(n-1) small-sample correction is applied.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": 2,
   "source": [
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "Final analysis: wealth-inequality change, white F vs white M, 1990 vs 1996.\n",
    "Headline = Lorenz-curve Gini (handles negatives naturally via rank ordering).\n",
    "Supporting: std, CV, IQR, P90/P50, top-decile share.\n",
    "Bootstrap 1000-iteration 95% CIs (percentile method).\n",
    "Winsorized (1/99) and ever_jailed=0 robustness variants.\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "import json\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "RNG = np.random.default_rng(20261021)\n",
    "BOOT_N = 1000\n",
    "\n",
    "DATA = Path('/workspace/data/nls_incarceration_processed.csv')\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(DATA)\n",
    "white = df[df['race'] == 'white'].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# ----- Lorenz-curve (rank-based) Gini: well-defined for any real-valued vector\n",
    "# whose sum is strictly positive. With debt-as-negative-values, this places\n",
    "# observations with negative wealth at the bottom of the cumulative-wealth\n",
    "# Lorenz curve, which is the conventional treatment in inequality economics.\n",
    "def gini(x):\n",
    "    x = np.asarray(x, dtype=float)\n",
    "    n = x.size\n",
    "    if n < 2: return float('nan')\n",
    "    x_sorted = np.sort(x)\n",
    "    total = x_sorted.sum()\n",
    "    if total <= 0: return float('nan')\n",
    "    cum = np.cumsum(x_sorted)\n",
    "    L = cum / total\n",
    "    x_axis = np.linspace(1.0/n, 1.0, n)\n",
    "    area = np.trapezoid(L, x_axis)\n",
    "    G = 1.0 - 2.0 * area\n",
    "    # small-sample correction for empirical Gini\n",
    "    G_emp = G * n / (n - 1)\n",
    "    return float(G_emp)\n",
    "\n",
    "def cv(x):\n",
    "    return float(np.std(x, ddof=1) / abs(np.median(x))) if np.median(x) != 0 else float('nan')\n",
    "\n",
    "def iqr(x):\n",
    "    return float(np.percentile(x, 75) - np.percentile(x, 25))\n",
    "\n",
    "def p90_p50(x):\n",
    "    p50 = np.median(x)\n",
    "    return float(np.percentile(x, 90) / p50) if p50 != 0 else float('nan')\n",
    "\n",
    "def top_decile_share(x):\n",
    "    x = np.asarray(x, dtype=float)\n",
    "    cutoff = np.percentile(x, 90)\n",
    "    top = x[x >= cutoff]\n",
    "    s = x.sum()\n",
    "    return float(top.sum() / s) if s != 0 else float('nan')\n",
    "\n",
    "def compute_metrics(x):\n",
    "    x = np.asarray(x, dtype=float)\n",
    "    return dict(\n",
    "        n=int(x.size),\n",
    "        mean=float(x.mean()),\n",
    "        median=float(np.median(x)),\n",
    "        std=float(x.std(ddof=1)),\n",
    "        cv=cv(x),\n",
    "        iqr=iqr(x),\n",
    "        p90_p50=p90_p50(x),\n",
    "        gini=gini(x),\n",
    "        top10_share=top_decile_share(x),\n",
    "        pct_zero=float((x == 0).mean() * 100),\n",
    "        pct_neg=float((x < 0).mean() * 100),\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "# Pretty-print\n",
    "def print_metrics(label, m):\n",
    "    print(f\"{label:<22}  n={m['n']:>4}  mean={m['mean']:>10.0f}  med={m['median']:>8.0f}  \"\n",
    "          f\"std={m['std']:>9.0f}  CV={m['cv']:>5.2f}  IQR={m['iqr']:>9.0f}  \"\n",
    "          f\"P90/P50={m['p90_p50']:>6.2f}  Gini={m['gini']:>6.3f}  \"\n",
    "          f\"top10%={m['top10_share']:>5.3f}  %0={m['pct_zero']:>4.1f}  %-={m['pct_neg']:>4.1f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "def bootstrap_ci(x, fn, n_iter=BOOT_N, alpha=0.05, rng=RNG):\n",
    "    x = np.asarray(x, dtype=float); n = x.size\n",
    "    stats = np.empty(n_iter, dtype=float)\n",
    "    for i in range(n_iter):\n",
    "        idx = rng.integers(0, n, n)\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            stats[i] = fn(x[idx])\n",
    "        except Exception:\n",
    "            stats[i] = np.nan\n",
    "    stats = stats[~np.isnan(stats)]\n",
    "    lo, hi = np.percentile(stats, [100*alpha/2, 100*(1-alpha/2)])\n",
    "    return float(np.mean(stats)), float(lo), float(hi), stats\n",
    "\n",
    "def winsorize(x, lo_p=1.0, hi_p=99.0):\n",
    "    lo, hi = np.percentile(x, [lo_p, hi_p]); return np.clip(x, lo, hi)\n",
    "\n"
   ],
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
